{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>All</b> — \"Everything came and reached thus\" is written in the book. And do not marvel that he did not write it about himself but only about Nebuchadnezzar, like (1 Samuel 12:11): \"And YHWH sent Jerubbaal and Bedan and Jephthah and Samuel,\" and He is the one counted. And so is the usage of הוה. Also עֲנֵה מַלְכָּא — as if he said \"I answered.\" And likewise בְּפוֹם מַלְכָּא."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The comment cites a reading 'in the book'; possibly referring to a specific manuscript or edition. The Aramaic phrases ענה מלכא and בפום מלכא are quoted from the Aramaic text of Daniel and left untranslated in Hebrew script, consistent with Ibn Ezra's practice of citing the lemma."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:19:57.121462787Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}